== A. sigma inside the Sturmian monoid <E, phi, phit> ==
E o phi o phi o phit o E = {'a': 'cac', 'c': 'cacac'}  equals sigma: True
q = E o phit o E: True ; q' := E o phi o E = {'a': 'c', 'c': 'ca'} = mirror of q: True
sigma = q' o q' o q: True
q^3 = {'a': 'cac', 'c': 'accac'} ; sigma(x).cac == cac.q^3(x) for x in {a,c}: True
matrix(sigma) = ((1, 2), (2, 3)) (rows #a,#c; columns images of a,c) = Q^3 = [[F2,F3],[F3,F4]]
distinct morphisms in <E,phi,phit> (words of length <= 7) with matrix Q^3: 7  (Seebold: |f(a)|+|f(c)|-1 = 7)
conjugate chain f_0..f_6 (f_{i+1}(x) = f_i(x) with first letter moved to the end):
   f_0: a->cac  c->cacca  in St: True  
   f_1: a->acc  c->accac  in St: True  
   f_2: a->cca  c->ccaca  in St: True  
   f_3: a->cac  c->cacac  in St: True  = sigma both images palindromes
   f_4: a->acc  c->acacc  in St: True  
   f_5: a->cca  c->cacca  in St: True  
   f_6: a->cac  c->accac  in St: True  = q^3
set of chain == set found: True
the 8 words of length 3 in {q, q'} and the conjugate they give:
   q o q o q    -> f_6
   q o q o q'   -> f_3
   q o q' o q   -> f_4
   q o q' o q'  -> f_1
   q' o q o q   -> f_5
   q' o q o q'  -> f_2
   q' o q' o q  -> f_3
   q' o q' o q' -> f_0
each f_i maps the length-3000 prefix of a Sturmian word to a balanced word: True

